{
 "description": "DEP-03 Replacement collateral declaration: the coin a member pledges in a DisputeArmed. Its own earlier pledge for this dispute while unspent; else the smallest coin with at least max(1, min_confs) confirmations that covers need and that no other live arm of the member pledges (taken), ties to the lexicographically smaller outpoint; else none. A coin pledged to two disputes is spent by whichever claim lands first and strands the other (regtest rearm-rust 1119-100553, deposits-rust). Shared by cl-deposits (inspect/lottery-test.lisp, pick-pledge) and deposits-rust (dispute.rs, pick_pledge). Cases with `forks` add what each of the member's forks still holds to `taken` (DEP-03, a pledge is held while its dispute is live): a fork's `ops` are its own DisputeEnter (`enter`), DisputeArmed (`arm`, with the `pledge` it declares or null), DisputeYield (`yield`, also the tombstone a lost lottery leaves) and DisputeAcquire (`acquire`, output 0 of `claim` and whether it `binds`). An `arm` may carry its `round` (TLV 366; 1 when absent). A fork's `others` are the DisputeAcquires by OTHER participants of its dispute, each with the `round` its claim closes and whether it `binds` (DEP-06 acquire_binding.json). A pledge is held from its arm until a later yield, a binding acquire of ours, a binding acquire by another participant for the arm's round or a later one, or the fork's retirement (`retired`); output 0 of a binding claim is custody, held while that acquire stands. Regtest 1120-next4: ref6 held 31 coins and could pledge none, 30 held by disputes long ended.",
